 Do not rely on hidden UI controls as authorization.
 
+### Tenant session
+
+A user works inside one entity at a time. `session('current_entity_id')` holds it,
+and **only the HTTP layer reads it**: the `current_entity` route middleware
+(`App\Http\Middleware\EnsureCurrentEntity`) resolves it into the per-request
+`App\Support\CurrentEntity` context (entity + membership) and aborts `403` when
+the user is not a member. With an empty session it dispatches on the number of
+memberships: none → `onboarding`, one → set the session and continue, several →
+`entity.switcher`. `GET /home` dispatches the same way (one entity → its
+dashboard). `POST /e/{entity:slug}/pick` switches entity (membership checked,
+written to the `audit` log). Policies: `App\Policies\EntityPolicy` and
+`EntityMembershipPolicy`.
+
 ## Source of truth
 
 | Concern | Source of truth |
